WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.612
Every management tool reports in its
own format against its own inventory.

2
00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:08.183
Five tools, five inventories,
and when an assessor asks

3
00:00:08.183 --> 00:00:11.437
you to prove a fix across
the whole estate, you can't.

4
00:00:11.437 --> 00:00:16.056
The answer is an evidence contract:
every source emits the same record,

5
00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:21.151
joined on one authoritative identity
for each asset, plus synchronized time.

6
00:00:21.151 --> 00:00:23.771
That identity has to come from one place,

7
00:00:23.771 --> 00:00:26.550
the naming plane, not
from each tool's own ID.

8
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.181
So the decision: stand up the naming plane
before you build the evidence pipeline,

9
00:00:31.181 --> 00:00:33.738
and write the contract
into the logging plan.

10
00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:39.224
The CISO owns the plan; the DNS and
identity teams own the naming plane.

11
00:00:39.224 --> 00:00:41.590
Next, where telemetry comes from.
